;; tedai (手代) app capability + synthetic-input stance registry — :representative (R0, G8).
;; Each record drives adapter-tier selection (T1 scripting/accessibility-API preferred) and the
;; G2 stance gate. Axes:
;;   :app/t1-available — the app exposes an official automation surface (AppleScript/JXA +
;;                       AXUIElement, Windows UI Automation, AT-SPI2/D-Bus, or its own CLI).
;;   :app/t2-stance    — the SYNTHETIC-INPUT stance (:permitted / :restricted / :prohibited); a
;;                       :prohibited stance refuses the T2 vision-pointer adapter by construction
;;                       (G2), EVEN where T2 would technically work. Missing → :prohibited
;;                       (default-deny input injection). Anti-cheat games + DRM players are the
;;                       canonical :prohibited case.
;;   :app/route        — surface owned by a sibling actor: browser apps route to :karakuri (N7 —
;;                       one owner per surface; tedai never re-implements web automation).
;; This is policy/capability data, NOT an endorsement. tedai operates only the MEMBER's OWN
;; physically-paired device (G1) and holds no pairing key (G3). Stances are :representative and
;; MUST be operator-verified before any live use (G6).
[{:app/id "finder"
  :app/name "Finder"
  :app/category :file-manager
  :app/t1-available true
  :app/t1-surface "applescript+ax"
  :app/t2-stance :permitted
  :app/tier :t1-scripting-api
  :app/representative true}

